All 61 pass, including the new [REDACTED_SECRET] test. Committed and clean.

## Summary

Found and fixed two real, distinct regressions in Melody's practice loop, both reported from live testing:

1. **Dead idle-timeout.** My earlier fix (making the drilled segment grow immediately on every correct note) had a side effect: the 2-second "no input → replay the segment" reminder was only ever scheduled from the "at the frontier" branch, which stopped being an occasional state and became the permanent state after every single correct play. Result: the reminder became silently unreachable — no more timeout, no more replay, no way to recall what came next without already knowing the song. Fixed by scheduling it unconditionally after every correct play.

2. **Silent same-pitch highlight ([REDACTED_SECRET]).** `Render.highlightByMidi`'s "restart the flash" trick used a forced synchronous reflow between removing and re-adding the CSS class — which never actually let the browser paint the "off" frame. Two notes at the same pitch played back-to-back (Happy Birthday's opening "Happy Happy") sounded as two distinct notes but showed as one continuous highlight. Verified this precisely with a frame-by-frame test before and after. Fixed by yielding two real animation frames between removing and re-adding the class.

Both confirmed red-then-green against the actual old code, both now covered by permanent tests. Full suite (unit tests, 216 desktop, 61 invariants) is green.

The "doesn't show the next note" complaint tested out as working correctly on its own (verified the glow does track the correct next-target pitch after each play) — most likely it just wasn't noticeable without the reminder replay, which is now fixed.

Separately, noted but not investigated: you flagged that the bug-report replay bundles far more session history than the current mode — that's a distinct issue I haven't looked at.


