### 2026-08-22T18:25:54.254Z | claude (claude-sonnet-5) | claude | conversation 627637ca-d250-4ad7-8a24-ddd841e171dd

Yes, exactly — that's the design. Concretely:

- `playFlourish()`'s state gains an explicit **[REDACTED_PRIVATE_INFO]** (e.g. `state.flourishStep`), not just a queue of already-scheduled timeouts. "Which note plays next" becomes real, inspectable state, the same way `snake`/`direction`/`score` already are — not something implicit in a closure that only exists inside a pending `setTimeout`.
- Pausing — whether via the Pause button or via `cleanup()` on a mode switch — just clears the one pending chained timeout and stops there. `isFlourishing` and `flourishStep` stay exactly as they were; nothing is lost or force-completed.
- Resuming — via the Pause button's toggle, or via `SnakeMode.init()` on returning to Snake (which today already skips `reset()` and just rebinds/repaints when a game is in progress) — reschedules the *next* step from `flourishStep`, timed fresh from the moment of resume, not from the original eat. So a real 10-minute pause mid-flourish doesn't queue up a timing pileup; it just continues cleanly, one 100ms step at a time, whenever you come back.
- Since `SnakeMode.state` is a plain singleton object that mode-switching never tears down, switching to Gravity and back doesn't need any special-case handling beyond that — the flourish [REDACTED_PRIVATE_INFO] is just sitting there in state like everything else, exactly like an in-progress (paused) normal move already survives a mode switch today.

So: pause mid-flourish → unpause → same flourish continues from the same note, correct spacing. Switch to Gravity → switch back to Snake → unpause → same spot in the game, mid-flourish included. That's the behavior I'll write the regression test against before touching `playFlourish`/`cleanup`.


