I've just launched a new search script (`[REDACTED_SECRET]`) that takes a completely different approach based on the geometry of the Hex grid. Instead of manually colliding puffers, it generates random seed soups but mathematically enforces either **180-degree (2-fold)**, **120-degree (3-fold)**, or **60-degree (6-fold)** rotational symmetry before running them.

